th the idea that  um maybe  maybe it was the wrong decision it's  done now isn't that you know we're  near enough all the way through it's got  to kind of  all those i know it kind of sounds silly  but you've made your bed now you've got  to kind of lie in it isn't it as long as  it's gone on and we've actually heard  the politicians talking government they  don't know  they're arguing once themselves it's  actually embarrassing  the prime minister is having a hard  enough time selling her chequers plan to  european leaders but our poll suggests  it doesn't have support  at home more people than ever want a  second referendum  and our study finds that question would  ultimately lead  to the uk staying in the european union  jason farrell sky news
 

